  "id": "tuning-curve",
  "term": "tuning curve",
  "definition": "A tuning curve is a function that shows how a sensory neuron’s response changes across values of a continuous stimulus dimension, such as sound frequency or visual orientation. It is used to describe which stimulus values produce stronger or weaker neural responses.",
